    "narrative": "Today\u2019s lineup for the **Austin Waves** is anchored by the exceptional matchup upside of **Gunnar Henderson**, who earns our highest daily score (81.87) against Hunter Brown. **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a strong platoon advantage and a favorable batting order position, making him the definitive centerpiece for our offensive output. We are also leaning heavily into the soft matchup against Jacob Lopez, providing significant boosts to both **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (66.11) and **Nasim Nunez** (67.37). While **Nasim Nunez** typically bats lower in the order, the combination of park factors and the pitcher\u2019s weak xERA creates a high-floor scenario that makes him an essential start for our pursuit of stolen base volume.\n\nBeyond the core, **Sam Antonacci** (67.67) and **Miguel Vargas** (63.05) project as high-value plays against Trey Yesavage, as both hitters capitalize on an inflated SP_xERA and favorable park dimensions. On the periphery of the lineup, **Jackson Merrill** (54.45) carries a marginal score, complicated by a 45% rain risk in his matchup against Noah Cameron; we will monitor this closely, as any delay or cancellation could force a pivot. The most difficult personnel decision today involved **Curtis Mead**, who nearly cracked the starting nine with a score of 58.98. Ultimately, the optimizer prioritized the higher ceiling of **Miguel Vargas** and the specialized platoon utility provided by **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, leaving **Curtis Mead** on the bench despite his favorable conditions against Jacob Lopez. We remain cautious with **Heliot Ramos** (41.88) and **Liam Hicks** (41.08), as both face difficult arms in Logan Gilbert and Robert Gasser, respectively, pushing them toward the lower end of our daily efficiency threshold.",
